  "title": "The playground and community got one home",
  "summary": "Pollinations brought its playground and community into one home while giving builders more control over images, app access, and the API details that make integrations work.\n\nThe themeable site brought Play, the theme creator, app directory, community page, and docs together at pollinations.ai. Play gained login controls, permission-aware model choices, up to four reference-image URLs, and clearer API errors. A grayscale preset, layout fixes, and browser-language translation made the new home more usable.\n\nVeo can generate between supplied first and last frames, while Z-Image Turbo generates at the requested resolution up to its dimension cap. `gptimage-large` joined the image API for generation and editing, then received fixes for reference-image edits, oversized inputs, and output aspect ratios. Fewer surprises between the prompt and the pixels.\n\nThird-party apps gained an authorization flow where users can review the app hostname and choose which models it may use. Model-list endpoints now reflect model-restricted keys, and `/v1/models` returns an OpenAI-compatible list response. Play also uses the signed-in user’s model access, so its selector matches what they can generate.\n\nMCP v2 moved to the unified API and added tools for video, parallel images, media analysis, transcription, search, tool-calling chat, and pricing lookup. The gateway now tolerates extra path segments from OpenAI-compatible clients; Gemini tool schemas and thinking settings received compatibility fixes. DeepSeek moved to V3.2, model lookups became case-insensitive, and failed image-URL conversion now stops a text request rather than sending partial input.",
